extraction_notes: "WB19 Australia printed 59-61 (cache p060-p062, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer in column order, with the special abilities on printed 60 checked against a render. Heading Bushranger O.C.C. on printed 59; Special Abilities on printed 60-61; the stat block on printed 61. || GROUP: listed under Outback O.C.C.s on printed 56 as Bushranger (criminal) O.C.C.; occ_group is optional. The entry prints Base S.D.C.: 4D6, stored as sdc_base. Not tagged evil: the alignment line allows any alignment. || XP: the Bushranger, Runabout, Infantry Grunt & City Police ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 224, read off a render. || BONUSES: +2 to roll with punch, fall or impact stored. || SPECIAL AREA OF EXPERTISE: the player chooses one of nine; stored as a pick-one special_abilities group. Applied as numbers: Extra Tough +1D4x10+20 S.D.C. (the text layer prints !D4xlO+20, confirmed on the render), Fast +3 initiative, +1 P.P., +3D6 Spd, Charmer +1D6 P.B. and +1D6 M.A. The book prints the Fast heading as East; it is read as Fast from its own text. NOT applied, in the option text only: every skill an option grants (Horseman: Horsemanship: Cowboy and one piloting skill +15%; Survivalist: Nature Lore, Blend, Trap/Mine Detection +15% and +5% Outback Survival; Expert Boxman: Mechanical Engineer, Locksmith, Demolitions, Demolitions Disposal +15%, +5% Pick Locks and Safecracking 20% +4%; Charmer: Seduction +30%; Impersonator: Imitate Voices/Impersonation, Art, Disguise +25%), the Gunman weapon-conditional attack and strike, the Horseman mounted initiative and dodge, and the Psionic roll (01-50 minor, 51-00 major, powers per the Rifts RPG page 12, which this book does not reprint). Nature Lore has no catalog row. The catalog holds Safe-Cracking at 20/4, the same figures as the Boxman special skill. || SKILL READINGS: Speaks Australian is Language: Australian English at 90 with the catalog per-level; Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic; General Athletics is Athletics (general); Pilot: Motorcycle or Hover Vehicle of choice is a pick among Motorcycles & Snowmobiles, Hover Craft (ground) and Hovercycles, Skycycles & Rocket Bikes; Horsemanship: Basic is Horsemanship: General (the book skill list has no Basic); W.P. Pistol is W.P. Automatic Pistol; W.P. Automatic Rifle is W.P. Automatic and Semi-automatic Rifles. Hand to Hand: Expert to start, Martial Arts or Assassin if evil for one related skill. || RELATED: Electrical Basic only is Basic Electronics; Mechanical except Robot or Aircraft excludes Robot Mechanics and Aircraft Mechanics; Science Math only is Mathematics: Basic and Advanced; Pilot except Robot Elite and military vehicles excludes the Robot Combat Elite rows, the Military: rows and Fighter Combat. The book files Horsemanship under Pilot (printed 151-152); the catalog has its own category, offered as General and Exotic Animals at the Pilot +5%. || SECONDARY: two at levels 1, 3, 6, 10 and 13. || MONEY: 2D4x$200 in dollars is starting_money; Australian dollars equal credits. The 1D6x$1000 in saleable items (the text layer prints lD6x$1000) is goods, in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT: the homespun M.D.C. armor is a pick among the five M.D.C. homespun body armors; the saber may be a Vibro-Blade, a pick of two; the mount is a pick of riding horse or hovercycle. The 1D4+2 M.D. explosives of any kind are stored on the hand grenade row and the 1D4 S.D.C. explosives (1D6x10 S.D.C.; text layer !D6xlO) on the dynamite row, both readings of an open choice. NOT stored as rows: the pair of sidearms (revolvers or pistols) with three full reloads each, the rifle appropriate to the W.P. with four reloads, broad brim hat, equipment webbing, notebook or notebook computer and ground blanket; they are in GM Notes."
---

## Lore

Grand name aside, a Bushranger is a criminal. The tradition goes back to the
continent''s days as a penal colony: lone outlaws or gangs of three to ten who
held up coaches and banks and raided trading posts, mining camps, towns and
rich estates. After the Cataclysm threw Australia back to something like its
early days, they returned bolder than ever.

Bushrangers live for the moment. They are not careless; they are deadly
serious about the work and accept its risks, but they seldom plan ahead,
preferring a fast decision and a lightning raid when a chance appears. They
strike from the wild and vanish back into it, relying on mobility, surprise,
distraction and disguise, and many hide a second life as an ordinary citizen.

The Outback cannot agree about them. Some rob the rich to help the poor,
fight Roadgangers and monsters, or stand up for a town; others rob, pillage
and kill for profit or pleasure. Either way they are well-trained,
well-equipped fighters, and each builds a reputation on one signature talent.

## GM Notes

Choose one Special Area of Expertise at creation. The sheet applies only the
flat numbers (Extra Tough, Fast, Charmer). Everything else is added by hand:

- Gunman: +1 attack with revolvers or rifles, no penalty for shooting on the
  move, +1 to strike with them in every mode; or, G.M. permitting, the
  Gunfighter abilities from Rifts New West page 91.
- Horseman: Horsemanship: Cowboy and one piloting skill at +15%; +2 initiative
  and +1 dodge while riding that animal or vehicle.
- Survivalist: Nature Lore, Blend and Trap/Mine Detection at +15%; +5% Outback
  Survival.
- Expert Boxman: Mechanical Engineer, Locksmith, Demolitions and Demolitions
  Disposal at +15%; +5% Pick Locks; Safecracking 20% +4% per level (-10% with
  an M.E. under 15).
- Charmer: Seduction at +30%; +5% Disguise and Impersonation if held.
- Impersonator: Imitate Voices/Impersonation, Art and Disguise at +25%.
- Psionic: roll percentile; 01-50 minor psionic, 51-00 major psychic, powers
  chosen as the Rifts RPG page 12 describes.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: a pair of sidearms (revolvers or
pistols) with three full reloads each, a rifle matching the character''s W.P.
with four reloads, a broad brim hat, equipment webbing, a notebook or notebook
computer and a ground blanket. The homespun armor is not fully environmental.

Money: besides the cash, 1D6x$1000 in saleable items of any kind of valuable.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'bushranger');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'bushranger';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-bushranger-class.sql');
